      "title": "IBM ContextForge MCP Gateway: DNS-rebinding SSRF in /llmchat/connect reaches loopback MCP tools",
      "descriptions": [
        {
          "lang": "en",
          "value": "ContextForge MCP Gateway (mcp-contextforge-gateway) 1.0.0-RC2 through 1.1.1 validates the user-supplied MCP server URL in POST /llmchat/connect once, then passes the hostname to the streamable-HTTP transport, which resolves it again. A DNS name with TTL 0 can answer with a public address during validation and 127.0.0.1 during the transport lookup. The gateway then connects to a loopback MCP server, returns its tool list in the connect response, and invokes its tools through POST /llmchat/chat. Any authenticated account with the default developer role (llm.invoke) is sufficient. Versions 0.9.0 through 1.0.0-RC1 are also affected by direct SSRF because the endpoint lacked outbound URL validation. Fixed in 1.1.2."
        }
      ],
      "affected": [
        {
          "vendor": "IBM",
          "product": "ContextForge MCP Gateway",
